      "id": "s2",
      "concept": "Mass",
      "narration": "Mass is a measure of how much matter is in an object. It is measured in kilograms and remains constant regardless of location. In Newton's second law, mass appears in the denominator, so larger mass means smaller acceleration for the same force.",
