    {
      "id": "s3",
      "concept": "acceleration",
      "narration": "Acceleration is how fast an object's velocity changes over time. It's measured in metres per second squared, or m/s^2. For example, if a car speeds up from 0 to 10 m/s in 2 seconds, its acceleration is 5 m/s^2.",
